{"cluster_id": "C-1990", "topic": "GC fold body reads should size", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B014-034"], "canonical_claim": "GC fold body reads should size each fresh `ReadBufferFromS3` from the known listed/meta body size plus small slack, capped at the current default; the expected effect is approximately 99% less fold-buffer churn with no behavior change.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-13-cas-memory-s3-budget-optimizations-design.md#s1-fold-buffers"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1991", "topic": "Manifest debris must be drained before", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B014-047"], "canonical_claim": "Manifest debris must be drained before deleting the victim mount slot because deleting the mount body removes `floorForNamespace` watermark authority and would make the debris ineligible forever; the decommission command is the epoch authority and can sweep old-epoch prefixes.", "issue_ids": ["B200"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-13-cas-pool-member-decommission.md#L487-L641"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1992", "topic": "The rev 6 GC defense audit", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B014-080"], "canonical_claim": "The rev.6 GC-defense audit treats zero S3 requests spent fighting a foreign writer on hot paths as the compliance principle; incidental checks and CAS-linearized commits are compliant by definition.", "issue_ids": ["rev.6"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-13-cas-ref-lease-exclusivity-rev6.md#task-13"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1993", "topic": "A new GC leader starts lease", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B015-017"], "canonical_claim": "A new GC leader starts lease observation afresh, delaying fencing by one round without weakening safety because fencing is a liveness and cleanup mechanism.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-13-cas-ref-lease-exclusivity-rev6-design.md#gc-fence-out"]}
