{"cluster_id": "C-1998", "topic": "CAS runs use sorted NDJSON with", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B016-029"], "canonical_claim": "CAS runs use sorted NDJSON with no blocks, footer, or `seek`; `RunFileReader::seek`, `inDegreeInGeneration`, and `SourceEdgeKeyCodec::seekPrefix` are deleted because production consumers read runs sequentially, accepting approximately twice the bytes with re-binarizing `cas_run` as the localized fallback.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-15-cas-codecs-v3-design.md#container-design"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1999", "topic": "cas_gc_outcomes is not deterministic it uses", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B016-065"], "canonical_claim": "`cas_gc_outcomes` is not deterministic: it uses idempotent `putIfAbsent`, and replay adopts an existing durable object after decoding rather than treating byte inequality as a correctness failure.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-15-cas-codecs-v3-phase2-control-plane.md#task5"]}
